TI  - Comparison of immunoturbidimetric and immunonephelometric assays for specific 
      proteins.
PG  - 1568-71
LID - 10.1016/j.clinbiochem.2009.06.016 [doi]
AB  - Immunoturbidimetric assays for specific proteins are available on "open system" 
      clinical chemistry analyzers. The analytical performance of nine 
      immunoturbidimetric specific protein assays (C3, C4, CRP, Haptoglobin, IgA, IgG, 
      IgM, RF, and Transferrin) was compared to immunonephelometry. Testing was 
      performed on the Abbott ARCHITECT ci8200 and the Dade Behring BNII nephelometer 
      and evaluated for precision, linearity, limit of detection, prozone phenomenon, 
      method comparison, workflow, and proficiency testing survey comparison. 
      Immunoturbidimetric assays performance was satisfactory for total precision, 
      linearity, limit of detection and the prozone effect was not observed. Method 
      comparison was acceptable for the immunoglobulins, CRP and transferrin but less 
      favorable for the other assays, likely due to methodology and antibody 
      specificity differences. Immunourbidimetric specific protein assays allow for 
      efficient test consolidation on a general purpose clinical chemistry analyzer.
